  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 126 AM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nHigh temperatures today will be 10 to 15 degrees above normal\nwith readings mostly in the upper 80s. Increasing clouds tonight\nwill result in warmer overnight lows in the upper 50s to around\n60 degrees.\n\nThe center of the remnants of Isaias is currently forecast to \nmove through Alabama, into middle Tennessee by 12z Sunday, then\ninto eastern Kentucky by early Monday. The model blend spreads \n30-60% chances of showers into most of west Kentucky and extreme\nsoutheast Missouri Saturday morning. By Saturday afternoon, \n50-100% chances of showers will spread across the entire PAH fa,\ncontinuing into Saturday evening. The best potential for some \nthunderstorms Saturday afternoon will be in west Kentucky, then \nSaturday evening across west Kentucky, southwest Indiana and \nsoutheast Illinois. Shower chances will gradually taper off \nfrom west to east late Saturday night into Sunday morning, with \ndry conditions across the entire area by Sunday afternoon.\n\nThe farther east track of Isaias remnants continues to minimize\nany real concerns across our area. Rain may be briefly heavy at\ntimes Saturday afternoon and evening, especially in west\nKentucky and southwest Indiana. Peak wind gusts during this \ntime period look to be 25-35mph, mainly across west Kentucky, \nextreme southeast Missouri, extreme southeast Illinois and \nsouthwest Indiana. Any threat of severe thunderstorms will be \nwell off to our southeast.\n\nTemperatures will be significantly cooler Saturday due to the\nclouds and rain, with highs in the 70s. Clouds decreasing from \nwest to east Sunday will allow temperatures to start warming \nback up, and by Monday readings will be right back up to 10 to \n15 degrees above normal in the middle 80s to near 90 degrees. \nWell above normal temperatures will continue through the week. \n\nOn Wednesday, models lift a warm front into our region, with a \ncold front approaching from the west on Thursday. The model \nblend produces 20-40% chances of mainly showers Wednesday into \nThursday, with an isolated thunderstorm possible.",
